1
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:09,809
(Hwang In Youp)

2
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:14,990
(Lee Hye Ri)

3
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:21,890
(Baek Sung Chul, Lee Yul Eum)

4
00:00:35,010 --> 00:00:39,079
(Dream To You)

5
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,080
(All people, events, and backgrounds are fictional.)

6
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,080
(This drama includes footage created using AI.)

7
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:42,080
(Children and animals were filmed under strict safety guidelines.)

8
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:48,050
Yi Jae.

9
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:50,460
What?

10
00:00:58,800 --> 00:00:59,860
That was dangerous.

11
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:02,800
Director Joo.

12
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:05,940
- Seong Moo? - Are you okay?

13
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,710
Who was it? Who did that?

14
00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:10,140
No, I just...

15
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:12,779
- I am sorry. - Hey, you idiot.

16
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:14,580
How often did I tell you not to run around?

17
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:16,610
Come on, I told you to be careful.

18
00:01:17,020 --> 00:01:20,390
Are you okay? You are bleeding.

19
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:24,820
I am fine. Yes. I am okay.

20
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:28,160
Looks like our Gyeongseong Love Song team...

21
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:29,430
is about to have a hit shoot.

22
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:31,930
Go see the medic team right now.

23
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,500
Hurry.

24
00:01:34,501 --> 00:01:37,140
Go to the medic station and get checked.

25
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:40,810
I told you to be careful.

26
00:01:43,170 --> 00:01:45,540
(Episode 9)

27
00:01:46,110 --> 00:01:49,250
Fortunately, it is just a scrape. It should not affect shooting.

28
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:50,320
Thank you.

29
00:01:50,650 --> 00:01:51,780
Thank you.

30
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:57,060
Your call time is not for a while. Why did you come so early?

31
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,320
And you get hurt the moment you arrive.

32
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:01,030
I guess this is why I came early.

33
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:03,700
What would you have done if I had not been there?

34
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:05,260
Right?

35
00:02:05,261 --> 00:02:06,760
An actor should take care of himself.

36
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:10,740
Director Joo.

37
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:13,540
How did you feel when you heard I was coming?

38
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:15,140
I was surprised.

39
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:18,080
I thought you would never want to see me again.

40
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:19,910
Why would I?

41
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:21,450
Well, I just...

42
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:24,280
I was not exactly a great girlfriend to you.

43
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:31,959
Oh, come on.

44
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:32,960
That punk...

45
00:02:33,930 --> 00:02:34,930
Darn it.

46
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:44,270
Director, everything is ready.

47
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:46,640
- Yes, I will be right there. - Yes.

48
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:50,440
- But... - Why you...

49
00:02:51,910 --> 00:02:53,140
Yes, Director.

50
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:56,710
Director Joo.

51
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:59,220
- Director Joo. - Why are you rushing me?

52
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,520
I am going.

53
00:03:02,850 --> 00:03:05,060
Sorry for the late introduction, Director Woo.

54
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,120
You look fine to me.

55
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:08,629
Since the introduction is already late, let us make it even later.

56
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:09,690
We have to go shoot now.

57
00:03:10,030 --> 00:03:12,260
- Let us go, Yi Jae. - I will see you later, Seong Moo.

58
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:14,530
Hey.

59
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,770
Why were you so familiar with him?

60
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,970
That war zone ex was Geum Seong Moo?

61
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:22,240
- How did you find out? - How could I not?

62
00:03:22,810 --> 00:03:26,040
I was going to tell you before he got here. I swear.

63
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:29,350
Stop with the sweet talk. What were you going to say?

64
00:03:29,810 --> 00:03:31,880
What, the guy who was dead and gone has come back to life?

65
00:03:31,950 --> 00:03:34,349
Well, when you break up with someone,

66
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:36,350
you just consider them dead and move on.

67
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:37,420
That is just basic courtesy...

68
00:03:37,490 --> 00:03:39,060
to the person you are currently with, right?

69
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,590
Gosh.

70
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:42,790
Gosh, you.

71
00:03:44,330 --> 00:03:45,330
What was that?

72
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:48,400
- What? - What was with that?

73
00:03:49,370 --> 00:03:51,470
- I guess I find you cute. - What is it?

74
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:53,910
"What is it?" Unbelievable.

75
00:03:55,770 --> 00:03:58,280
Hey! Stop!

76
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:24,400
Crow?

77
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:32,740
Cut.

78
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:35,080
Okay.

79
00:04:35,950 --> 00:04:36,950
That is a wrap.

80
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:39,020
- That is a wrap. - That is a wrap.

81
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,320
Are you okay?

82
00:04:41,550 --> 00:04:43,450
- Mu Gyeom. - Yes.

83
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,990
- Great, that was a good take. - Thank you.

84
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:46,060
You've improved a lot.

85
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:47,960
Director Woo.

86
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:50,730
I'm telling you, one more take and my shoulder would've given out.

87
00:04:51,030 --> 00:04:52,330
Thank you, DP.

88
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,270
It came out looking great, thanks to you.

89
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:12,349
- Hey, Sim Yu Geon. - Seong Moo!

90
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:13,750
You're starting to look like a real actor.

91
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:18,290
- It's been so long. - How have you been?

92
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,930
- Just a second. - It's so good to see you. Really.

93
00:05:25,230 --> 00:05:27,500
- You... - Are they that close?

94
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:29,700
It's nice to see. Why?

95
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:32,300
Everyone, today's lunch...

96
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:35,339
is on the independence army leader, Crow!

97
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:37,240
Everyone, head to the food truck.

98
00:05:40,450 --> 00:05:42,709
- Crow! - Crow!

99
00:05:42,710 --> 00:05:45,180
- Don't mention it. - Really, it's nothing.

100
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:46,549
You're the best, my Seong Moo.

101
00:05:46,550 --> 00:05:48,520
Well, it is Director Joo's set.

102
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:51,660
"My" Seong Moo?

103
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:54,860
- Yes. - What? Are you jealous?

104
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:55,990
What? Jealous?

105
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:57,730
Am I jealous of those two?

106
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:00,800
- No. I don't care. - Actor Geum!

107
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:05,470
It's really been a long time.

108
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:11,140
Seong Moo.

109
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,710
(Go, Gyeongseong Love Song! Congrats on the debut, Director Joo!)

110
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:15,650
Are you touched?

111
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,820
I've made it big, so I can do at least this much for you.

112
00:06:19,950 --> 00:06:21,150
Why did you have to go and get famous?

113
00:06:21,550 --> 00:06:23,590
What is this? This is so embarrassing.

114
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:25,660
How can you take three servings for yourself?

115
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:28,530
Thanks to Director Joo, I'm really living the high life.

116
00:06:28,590 --> 00:06:30,530
You have the golden touch. Thanks for the food.

117
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:33,299
No, it's not the golden touch, it's Golden Seong Moo. Am I right?

118
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:36,430
- Ms. Namgung Se Ra. - You're right, Mr. Gu Seok Gi.

119
00:06:37,940 --> 00:06:40,440
See? We have great banter. Come with me.

120
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:42,740
Our Director Joo is really blessed with good people.

121
00:06:43,270 --> 00:06:45,810
Your high school classmate is Director Woo.

122
00:06:46,010 --> 00:06:50,520
And your university alumnus is our Actor Geum. Gosh.

123
00:06:50,850 --> 00:06:52,350
(Please take good care of Yi Jae.)

124
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:54,090
He sounds a bit sarcastic.

125
00:06:54,390 --> 00:06:56,990
He's always like that. Let us eat too.

126
00:06:57,890 --> 00:07:00,630
Before that, let's get a picture. To prove you were here.

127
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:04,060
- A picture? No, it's fine. - Come on.

128
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:05,100
No, really.

129
00:07:07,670 --> 00:07:10,300
Congratulations. Make it cute.

130
00:07:11,370 --> 00:07:12,570
Oh, come on.

131
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,240
That's it, like this.

132
00:07:14,770 --> 00:07:18,640
Hey. Your cameo is a secret until the premiere.

133
00:07:18,710 --> 00:07:22,510
I know. I'll post it right when we need the publicity.

134
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:24,820
Do not worry. Cheese.

135
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:29,489
- Gosh. - Yi Jae hates that angle.

136
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:31,790
He's so bad at taking selfies. Unbelievable.

137
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:33,930
I told you so.

138
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:37,060
I told you she dated a really famous actor.

139
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,700
When did you say that?

140
00:07:39,230 --> 00:07:40,460
You just weren't listening.

141
00:07:41,070 --> 00:07:44,470
Gosh. Hey, "number one fan?" I'm the number one fan.

142
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:47,240
I cannot concede that to him, even if he is Seong Moo.

143
00:07:48,210 --> 00:07:50,310
Hey, right? Gosh.

144
00:07:50,370 --> 00:07:53,410
No, I'm her number one fan. Since I was in middle school.

145
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:54,880
Whatever.

146
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:57,720
But why are you so close with Geum Seong Moo?

147
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:00,180
The three of us used to hang out a lot.

148
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:04,090
We all hung out together. So why do you only like Geum Seong Moo?

149
00:08:04,190 --> 00:08:05,960
You said if Yi Jae dislikes someone, you do too, right?

150
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:08,660
Isn't that why you've been so hostile toward me?

151
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,860
Because there's no way she would ever dislike Seong Moo.

152
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,500
Why?

153
00:08:14,070 --> 00:08:17,470
Even when they broke up, he was a good person to her.

154
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:20,740
Unlike some people.

155
00:08:21,410 --> 00:08:22,410
Yu Geon.

156
00:08:22,670 --> 00:08:23,670
Yes?

157
00:08:24,810 --> 00:08:27,009
- Take a picture of Yi Jae and me? - Sure.

158
00:08:27,010 --> 00:08:29,250
Make sure you get the whole poster in the picture.

159
00:08:29,310 --> 00:08:30,510
He's a jerk too.

160
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:32,980
Okay, act natural.

161
00:08:33,450 --> 00:08:36,520
- Get a little closer, act natural. - A heart, like this, Director Joo.

162
00:08:36,590 --> 00:08:38,890
One, two...

163
00:08:43,090 --> 00:08:44,100
Director Woo.

164
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,600
- What is it? - A picture.

165
00:08:46,660 --> 00:08:48,970
- Oh, right. - Director, the line is over there.

166
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:52,440
- Oh, right. Take your picture. - Okay, let's try again.

167
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:58,280
- One, two... - But I find this a bit lacking.

168
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:01,250
Your head shot is a little cheesy.

169
00:09:03,380 --> 00:09:05,480
Why don't you get some new head shots?

170
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,490
What are you doing, Director Woo?

171
00:09:08,790 --> 00:09:09,790
What?

172
00:09:10,790 --> 00:09:12,590
Look. Isn't it a little different?

173
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:14,790
Look.

174
00:09:15,130 --> 00:09:18,960
The three of us...

175
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:21,899
eating food like this, it's really been a while, right?

176
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:23,870
That's right. When you helped Yi Jae with her film shoots,

177
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:25,240
gimbap was always a late-night snack.

178
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:27,240
Even though Seong Moo doesn't even like gimbap.

179
00:09:27,510 --> 00:09:29,870
You didn't like gimbap? You never said so.

180
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:34,180
How could he tell the person who always bought gimbap so bluntly?

181
00:09:34,350 --> 00:09:35,380
Oh, right.

182
00:09:36,010 --> 00:09:37,249
But that place closed down.

183
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:39,650
- Really? - Why? It was so good.

184
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:40,690
I know.

185
00:09:41,490 --> 00:09:43,650
That twisted doughnut shop we went to before...

186
00:09:43,690 --> 00:09:45,689
- is still there. Right? - Yes.

187
00:09:45,690 --> 00:09:48,929
Oh, right. The one in the market alley.

188
00:09:48,930 --> 00:09:50,230
That place is delicious.

189
00:09:54,530 --> 00:09:56,900
We only went there once, but he has a good memory.

190
00:09:58,570 --> 00:10:02,140
One visit was all it took. Joo Yi Jae, Darn it.

191
00:10:03,740 --> 00:10:05,710
What should we do?

192
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:09,250
There are only three seats.

193
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:14,650
- Director Woo and I'll eat outside. - Why?

194
00:10:15,390 --> 00:10:16,390
Let's eat together.

195
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,990
And I can give my belated greetings.

196
00:10:21,890 --> 00:10:24,900
- Could we borrow a chair? - Yes, Director.

197
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:25,960
Thank you.

198
00:10:30,330 --> 00:10:31,340
Sit down, Yi Jae.

199
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:57,830
Director Joo, you eat carrots now? You're all grown up.

200
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:59,660
He must not know the story behind the carrots.

201
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:01,370
He wouldn't be laughing like that otherwise.

202
00:11:03,070 --> 00:11:05,640
I'm over 30, so I can't be a picky eater.

203
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:09,440
Chew your food well, Director Joo. You don't want to get indigestion.

204
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:11,440
Hey.

205
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:14,080
It's weird to hear you call her "Director Joo."

206
00:11:14,150 --> 00:11:16,810
Why? She is Director Joo. Should he call her "Yi Jae" here?

207
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:17,880
It was her nickname.

208
00:11:30,090 --> 00:11:33,300
Wait. So did our nicknames become our titles?

209
00:11:34,670 --> 00:11:38,970
Then should you call me "Actor Geum" like back then?

210
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:42,210
You're not Actor Kim, so I should call you Actor Geum.

211
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:45,540
- I'm finished. May I be excused? - Director Joo.

212
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:48,280
You changed your number, right? Can you give it to me?

213
00:11:48,450 --> 00:11:51,480
You're only in three scenes, so why do you need her number?

214
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:54,119
Contact me. It's 010...

215
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:57,020
When I said "Director Joo" just now, it was a nickname.

216
00:11:57,150 --> 00:11:58,690
I'm asking her this personally.

217
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:07,830
It's just a phone number. It's fine. Yes, I'll put it in for you.

218
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:13,700
Here.

219
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:17,240
(Geum Seong Moo)

220
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:19,980
What? You already had my number, Director Joo.

221
00:12:20,310 --> 00:12:21,680
Why do I have this?

222
00:12:22,250 --> 00:12:24,920
Oh, it must have synced when I transferred everything...

223
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:26,250
from my old phone. Right?

224
00:12:26,550 --> 00:12:28,220
Right, that must be it.

225
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:32,360
Well, then. Thanks for the meal.

226
00:12:34,390 --> 00:12:35,830
Hey, wait. Wait for me.

227
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:39,360
Well, then.

228
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:45,540
Oh, right.

229
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:47,570
Put your chair back.

230
00:12:54,810 --> 00:12:55,810
Darn it.

231
00:12:59,750 --> 00:13:01,390
(Director Joo Yi Jae, Director Woo Su Bin)

232
00:13:01,450 --> 00:13:03,520
- Are you okay? - Director, we're ready.

233
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:06,820
Are you sure you can do this? It looks dangerous.

234
00:13:06,890 --> 00:13:08,160
I'm Geum Seong Moo.

235
00:13:10,090 --> 00:13:11,100
All right.

236
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:14,870
So, for the Crow's jump, it's not just a simple jump.

237
00:13:14,930 --> 00:13:16,830
It should feel more like you're taking flight.

238
00:13:16,970 --> 00:13:19,970
A big jump, like this. A really big jump.

239
00:13:21,670 --> 00:13:23,910
- A big jump? - I already told the coordinator.

240
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:24,980
- A big jump? - No.

241
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:27,810
It only looks ridiculous because I'm the one doing it.

242
00:13:28,010 --> 00:13:29,410
Anyway, you get what I mean, right?

243
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:34,190
Excuse me, is the actor's audio on right now?

244
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:35,450
I can't hear anything.

245
00:13:35,650 --> 00:13:37,290
Oh, it was turned off for the rehearsal.

246
00:13:37,350 --> 00:13:38,390
No, turn it on now!

247
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:42,689
I need to do a sound check with the wireless mic.

248
00:13:42,690 --> 00:13:43,730
Right now?

249
00:13:44,060 --> 00:13:45,530
There's nothing wrong with it.

250
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:48,300
Okay, fine.

251
00:13:49,230 --> 00:13:51,470
- Okay, it's on. - Yi Jae.

252
00:13:52,370 --> 00:13:53,540
It wasn't a mistake coming here, was it?

253
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:54,940
What?

254
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:58,139
Of course not. Why would you say that?

255
00:13:58,140 --> 00:14:01,349
You're the biggest star in the country right now.

256
00:14:01,350 --> 00:14:03,910
Can't you see how grateful I am?

257
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:05,950
Then why do you keep speaking so formally?

258
00:14:07,250 --> 00:14:08,250
Are you uncomfortable with me?

259
00:14:08,750 --> 00:14:09,750
Me?

260
00:14:10,990 --> 00:14:12,320
See? You just did it again.

261
00:14:15,130 --> 00:14:17,830
Am I the only one who's happy to see you again?

262
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,100
I was happy too...

263
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,130
to see you do so well for yourself.

264
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:23,400
"Happy"?

265
00:14:24,270 --> 00:14:27,970
- Wait, did she say she was happy? - Yes, I definitely heard that part.

266
00:14:28,370 --> 00:14:31,940
- But... - And honestly, I was also relieved.

267
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:35,950
- I could feel a little less sorry. - Is she talking to him informally?

268
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:37,580
You have nothing to be sorry for.

269
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:41,750
Yi Jae, I really cherished all the time we spent together.

270
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:45,820
That's why I was so excited to come to set today.

271
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:50,430
You dreamed of becoming a director, and now you are one.

272
00:14:50,630 --> 00:14:54,130
And I dreamed of becoming an actor, and now we're meeting again as one.

273
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:57,300
Come on. I still have a long way to go compared to you.

274
00:14:58,070 --> 00:14:59,440
You're so cool, Actor Geum.

275
00:15:01,770 --> 00:15:02,940
I missed it sometimes.

276
00:15:04,140 --> 00:15:07,440
Your voice when you'd call me "Actor Geum."

277
00:15:08,310 --> 00:15:09,310
What?

278
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,430
Yi Jae.

279
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:39,440
Let's just...

280
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:40,880
Let's just what?

281
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:44,080
Gosh, the wind today is just too much, right?

282
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:49,390
Get away from her.

283
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:54,120
Director, which one should we use for the Crow's gun?

284
00:15:58,900 --> 00:15:59,900
Nice.

285
00:16:00,930 --> 00:16:03,470
Gosh, Director Woo.

286
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:07,710
- You have so many talents. - I don't like it.

287
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:10,070
Then how about this one?

288
00:16:10,670 --> 00:16:11,740
We'll go with this one.

289
00:16:16,710 --> 00:16:19,250
Don't rub it. I'll blow on it.

290
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,050
Wait a moment.

291
00:16:21,950 --> 00:16:24,150
Look, this is making me uncomfortable.

292
00:16:24,690 --> 00:16:26,560
On set, I'd like it if we just...

293
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:29,390
treated each other as an actor and a director.

294
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,200
Okay.

295
00:16:35,130 --> 00:16:36,430
On set.

296
00:16:38,970 --> 00:16:40,970
Shall we? Director Joo.

297
00:16:41,410 --> 00:16:44,110
We're ready for rehearsal. We'll begin the Crow rehearsal.

298
00:16:44,210 --> 00:16:45,210
Okay.

299
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:47,310
Crow.

300
00:16:47,950 --> 00:16:49,850
Let's talk for a moment after the rehearsal.

301
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:52,550
Okay.

302
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:13,040
If I'd known you used to date Yi Jae,

303
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:15,370
I would have rejected your offer, Mr. Geum.

304
00:17:15,670 --> 00:17:18,140
Especially if I knew you were an ex who couldn't let her go.

305
00:17:18,210 --> 00:17:20,310
I couldn't let her go?

306
00:17:22,450 --> 00:17:23,610
Does Yi Jae know that?

307
00:17:24,850 --> 00:17:26,250
I hope she does.

308
00:17:29,450 --> 00:17:30,790
That's enough.

309
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:33,620
This is Yi Jae's workplace.

310
00:17:34,890 --> 00:17:36,890
The staff just thinks you two...

311
00:17:37,430 --> 00:17:40,230
are only high school classmates.

312
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:42,700
You don't seem to have any intention of hiding it from me, do you?

313
00:17:42,730 --> 00:17:44,300
You already know...

314
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:45,970
about Yi Jae and me.

315
00:17:48,070 --> 00:17:51,510
That you were her first love?

316
00:17:52,010 --> 00:17:53,480
I know about that much.

317
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:57,050
The reason Yi Jae and I started dating was...

318
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:00,080
It was thanks to you, Director Woo.

319
00:18:01,650 --> 00:18:04,460
Whenever Yi Jae drank...

320
00:18:04,690 --> 00:18:05,790
What was it she'd say?

321
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:08,060
That she and her first love...

322
00:18:08,690 --> 00:18:12,330
broke up without even a peck, so I gave her one.

323
00:18:13,030 --> 00:18:14,530
And I told her that she needs a first kiss...

324
00:18:16,570 --> 00:18:18,400
to forget a first love.

325
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,650
It must not have been a big deal.

326
00:18:29,850 --> 00:18:32,120
She told me you were some acting major who helped on a film shoot...

327
00:18:32,180 --> 00:18:33,480
That's all I heard.

328
00:18:33,950 --> 00:18:35,420
Then for these three scenes,

329
00:18:36,450 --> 00:18:40,220
it's a short time, but give us your best, Mr. Geum.

330
00:18:51,670 --> 00:18:55,510
Everyone, have some gimbap.

331
00:18:55,570 --> 00:18:56,970
Thank you.

332
00:18:57,840 --> 00:19:00,680
Geum Seong Moo is treating all of us to gimbap for lunch.

333
00:19:01,650 --> 00:19:02,910
Geum Seong Moo?`

334
00:19:04,180 --> 00:19:05,980
This is why I can't stand him.

335
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:07,850
If a cameo actor steals my thunder like that,

336
00:19:07,890 --> 00:19:09,220
what does that make me, the lead?

337
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:11,920
I was planning to treat everyone to a food truck soon.

338
00:19:11,990 --> 00:19:16,590
I know. That's why I've already laid the groundwork.

339
00:19:16,660 --> 00:19:18,130
I told them you have a plan too.

340
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,960
That when the staff is filming outside,

341
00:19:20,030 --> 00:19:21,969
and they feel cold and hungry,

342
00:19:21,970 --> 00:19:24,700
you're going to treat them to something huge.

343
00:19:24,770 --> 00:19:27,100
- I've already told everyone. - You're always so on top of things.

344
00:19:27,170 --> 00:19:28,440
Of course.

345
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:32,910
I may not be good at things like driving,

346
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:35,380
but this is why I get to stay by your side as your manager.

347
00:19:36,110 --> 00:19:37,550
I know.

348
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,490
This is so good.

349
00:19:42,490 --> 00:19:44,090
Hurry and have some.

350
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:47,490
I have to do a kiss scene. I'll eat after the scene.

351
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:49,730
Since when did you care about that?

352
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:51,630
Just eat. You can brush your teeth later.

353
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:55,300
No, it's fine. It wouldn't feel right.

354
00:20:01,310 --> 00:20:02,440
Sim Yu Geon.

355
00:20:03,340 --> 00:20:04,370
Come here.

356
00:20:07,010 --> 00:20:09,280
- Do we really have to do this? - Come on.

357
00:20:09,410 --> 00:20:12,350
Deal with it. I'm not thrilled about this either.

358
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:14,849
This is your first kiss scene. Like an action scene,

359
00:20:14,850 --> 00:20:17,150
a kiss scene needs to be choreographed.

360
00:20:17,820 --> 00:20:20,920
Focus. I'll go watch from over there.

361
00:20:23,490 --> 00:20:27,200
- Okay. - The space between them closes.

362
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,100
Their gazes lock.

363
00:20:29,430 --> 00:20:32,869
Nan Yeong. Take off Mu Gyeom's glasses...

364
00:20:32,870 --> 00:20:34,170
and look at him.

365
00:20:35,970 --> 00:20:37,270
Nan Yeong's line.

366
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:40,809
I thought only these glasses were blinding me,

367
00:20:40,810 --> 00:20:44,650
but what truly blinded my eyes was this longing in my heart.

368
00:20:47,950 --> 00:20:49,050
I love you.

369
00:20:51,150 --> 00:20:54,360
Mu Gyeom, focus. To Nan Yeong's confession,

370
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:56,190
Mu Gyeom slowly kisses her.

371
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:00,430
Slowly.

372
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:17,350
How about cupping her face with both hands?

373
00:21:17,410 --> 00:21:19,079
- Lower yourself a little more. - More?

374
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:20,250
- Yes. - Okay.

375
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,660
Mu Gyeom, look at Nan Yeong properly.

376
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:32,600
This feels a bit more poignant. Mu Gyeom, try it again.

377
00:21:37,030 --> 00:21:38,270
The kiss...

378
00:21:40,970 --> 00:21:42,840
What if Nan Yeong initiates it?

379
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:50,280
After all, she's confessing her love to her enemy.

380
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:55,250
I feel like this is the first moment she's taking charge of her own life.

381
00:21:55,990 --> 00:21:58,060
Couldn't this moment be the catalyst...

382
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:00,490
for her to eventually escape Wolhwajeong?

383
00:22:01,430 --> 00:22:03,959
So you're saying you want this kiss to be...

384
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:06,100
the first choice Nan Yeong makes for herself?

385
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,370
I guess that's something we missed.

386
00:22:12,070 --> 00:22:14,240
Then how about we try it as Nan Yeong suggested?

387
00:22:14,970 --> 00:22:15,970
I love it.

388
00:22:17,870 --> 00:22:19,110
Thank you.

389
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:20,740
Shall we try it then?

390
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,150
- I'll go down and watch. - Okay.

391
00:22:25,050 --> 00:22:27,820
The distance between them slowly closes.

392
00:22:28,820 --> 00:22:30,050
Their gazes lock.

393
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:35,060
Nan Yeong takes off Mu Gyeom's glasses and looks at him.

394
00:22:37,630 --> 00:22:41,670
I thought only these glasses were blinding me,

395
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:44,500
but what truly blinded my eyes...

396
00:22:45,340 --> 00:22:48,070
was this longing in my heart.

397
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:55,880
I love you.

398
00:22:58,420 --> 00:23:01,350
- This is so much better, right? - We can see Nan Yeong's emotions.

399
00:23:05,460 --> 00:23:06,620
Should I...

400
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:09,760
tilt my head this way?

401
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:13,500
This is infuriating.

402
00:23:15,070 --> 00:23:16,500
You don't remember that day, do you?

403
00:23:35,020 --> 00:23:36,320
Is this how I should do it?

404
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:39,590
Yes. It's good.

405
00:23:40,220 --> 00:23:42,790
If you just relax a little...

406
00:23:44,130 --> 00:23:46,060
Then I'll just touch up my lipstick and be right back.

407
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:47,600
Okay.

408
00:24:01,410 --> 00:24:03,280
How beautiful.

409
00:24:03,610 --> 00:24:05,980
Who ever heard of a kiss scene getting done in one take?

410
00:24:06,620 --> 00:24:09,390
- Our intense rehearsal paid off. - Yes.

411
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:14,660
So the shoot in Wolhwajeong set will be over in two days, right?

412
00:24:15,060 --> 00:24:16,160
I've grown attached to it.

413
00:24:17,090 --> 00:24:19,960
It is a shame to think it'll be over soon.

414
00:24:23,970 --> 00:24:25,899
Excuse me, Directors.

415
00:24:25,900 --> 00:24:28,670
Could I perhaps make a suggestion right now?

416
00:24:29,270 --> 00:24:31,410
Yes. Is there a problem?

417
00:24:31,780 --> 00:24:34,580
Everyone must be getting tired by now.

418
00:24:35,050 --> 00:24:36,510
We need a little refresher.

419
00:24:36,910 --> 00:24:38,750
He's right, Director.

420
00:24:39,020 --> 00:24:40,479
Let's go on a team-building trip.

421
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:43,150
We didn't even all get together during pre-production.

422
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:46,990
That's true. People usually go on a retreat before filming starts.

423
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:50,029
But don't the staff hate it...

424
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:52,260
when we all have to gather as a group?

425
00:24:52,460 --> 00:24:53,460
- Come on, that's not true. - Come on.

426
00:24:53,530 --> 00:24:55,730
If you prepare a lot of amazing prizes,

427
00:24:55,800 --> 00:25:00,300
- they'll scramble to go, right? - Of course. I want a refrigerator.

428
00:25:00,370 --> 00:25:02,370
What's with your obsession with a refrigerator?

429
00:25:02,510 --> 00:25:03,640
You're going on a retreat?

430
00:25:05,940 --> 00:25:07,640
Hey, you haven't left yet?

431
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:11,720
Hey, Comrade Mu Gyeom. Finished shooting?

432
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:16,790
Wait, what's with these two?

433
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:19,020
Ha Na.

434
00:25:19,890 --> 00:25:20,920
Long time no see.

435
00:25:21,790 --> 00:25:22,960
When did you get here?

436
00:25:23,060 --> 00:25:25,030
I'm the lead actress in this movie, you know.

437
00:25:25,100 --> 00:25:27,930
Oh, right. My bad.

438
00:25:28,730 --> 00:25:30,200
If you're going on a retreat,

439
00:25:30,270 --> 00:25:32,400
I can book the glamping site I go to often.

440
00:25:32,840 --> 00:25:34,970
- Let's go there. - That's awesome.

441
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:36,910
- Sounds good, right? - A Glamping Site? That sounds cool.

442
00:25:37,170 --> 00:25:40,810
- You're going too? - You think I'd just lend it to you?

443
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:42,109
Unbelievable.

444
00:25:42,110 --> 00:25:43,809
What kind of cameo actor pays for a food truck...

445
00:25:43,810 --> 00:25:45,080
and tags along on the team retreat?

446
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:46,319
You need to know when to get involved...

447
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:47,580
and when to stay out.

448
00:25:47,850 --> 00:25:50,090
Are you discriminating against guest actors now?

449
00:25:51,250 --> 00:25:54,490
To me, you are all already family.

450
00:25:54,560 --> 00:25:57,560
- Go, Gyeongseong Love Song! - Yes! Let's go!

451
00:25:57,590 --> 00:25:59,629
- Let him come. - He has to be the main character...

452
00:25:59,630 --> 00:26:02,500
wherever he goes. I really don't like him.

453
00:26:04,330 --> 00:26:05,900
We agree on something for once.

454
00:26:05,970 --> 00:26:10,510
Except for you two, it seems like everyone here wants me to come.

455
00:26:10,670 --> 00:26:11,780
Isn't that right, Director Joo?

456
00:26:12,110 --> 00:26:13,910
- Sorry? - I can come along, right?

457
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:15,750
Well...

458
00:26:24,120 --> 00:26:27,790
Yes, well... Let's all go together.

459
00:26:29,630 --> 00:26:32,500
- Yes. Let's go. - This will be fun.

460
00:26:42,340 --> 00:26:43,540
(Geum Seong Moo sent a photo.)

461
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:48,210
(Geum Seong Moo sent a photo.)

462
00:26:51,050 --> 00:26:54,080
Wait, why is this synced to my phone?

463
00:26:55,350 --> 00:26:56,350
Give it here.

464
00:26:56,720 --> 00:26:59,859
Hey. Let's at least respect each other's privacy.

465
00:26:59,860 --> 00:27:01,019
Privacy?

466
00:27:01,020 --> 00:27:03,290
Since when is Geum Seong Moo a part of your private life?

467
00:27:06,430 --> 00:27:09,630
This is the picture taken in front of that food truck.

468
00:27:09,670 --> 00:27:12,769
Look. There, you saw it, right?

469
00:27:12,770 --> 00:27:14,040
Now, focus on your driving.

470
00:27:14,670 --> 00:27:16,110
Whatever.

471
00:27:17,270 --> 00:27:20,840
"Whatever"? Gosh, Su Bin.

472
00:27:20,910 --> 00:27:23,480
- Such a cool guy. - I'm not cool.

473
00:27:24,410 --> 00:27:25,580
I realised that a person...

474
00:27:25,950 --> 00:27:27,120
can get so jealous...

475
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:29,690
that they could die.

476
00:27:30,920 --> 00:27:35,160
Why? Why are you jealous? You're the one I like, aren't you?

477
00:27:35,390 --> 00:27:38,290
It's just that he knows a version of you from a time...

478
00:27:38,360 --> 00:27:40,630
that I wasn't around for.

479
00:27:42,470 --> 00:27:45,170
And how cute you must have been.

480
00:27:45,300 --> 00:27:47,870
You must be jealous about it.

481
00:27:48,170 --> 00:27:50,610
But don't worry. I'm prettier now than I was in my 20s.

482
00:27:50,670 --> 00:27:52,440
That makes me even more anxious.

483
00:27:54,380 --> 00:27:56,910
When you went up on that bridge earlier...

484
00:27:58,750 --> 00:28:01,380
Never mind. I don't want to hear it.

485
00:28:01,750 --> 00:28:03,520
He's already getting on my nerves enough as it is.

486
00:28:06,760 --> 00:28:07,790
Joo Yi Jae.

487
00:28:09,560 --> 00:28:13,460
He might have been a good person to you, but I still don't like him.

488
00:28:14,030 --> 00:28:15,030
So...

489
00:28:15,700 --> 00:28:16,870
even if I'm being...

490
00:28:17,770 --> 00:28:19,670
a bit of a jerk,

491
00:28:21,910 --> 00:28:23,470
please try to understand.

492
00:28:29,950 --> 00:28:34,320
I'm a little better, aren't I? Is Geum Seong Moo...

493
00:28:35,650 --> 00:28:38,050
- more handsome? - No.

494
00:28:40,090 --> 00:28:42,259
- Okay. - You're handsome.

495
00:28:42,260 --> 00:28:43,330
- Me? - Yes.

496
00:28:43,390 --> 00:28:44,630
("Love Chain")

497
00:28:45,900 --> 00:28:48,199
- Have you eaten? - Go eat.

498
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:51,530
- Okay. - Seol, you should go eat too.

499
00:28:52,800 --> 00:28:55,610
- What's wrong? - I'm just so sad.

500
00:28:56,740 --> 00:28:58,410
Look at Hyo Rim over there.

501
00:28:58,710 --> 00:29:00,810
She was just rejected by the Catfish Man.

502
00:29:01,480 --> 00:29:03,680
He said he likes someone else.

503
00:29:07,550 --> 00:29:09,690
He said it's not me.

504
00:29:12,260 --> 00:29:14,820
There's nothing I can do.

505
00:29:16,860 --> 00:29:18,430
I'm so sad.

506
00:29:19,700 --> 00:29:22,530
It feels like my heart is being torn apart.

507
00:29:23,170 --> 00:29:26,740
Even I, the writer in charge, don't know what In Wook is thinking.

508
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:29,440
Imagine how frustrated Hyo Rim must feel.

509
00:29:32,910 --> 00:29:36,580
Why is she crying? There are plenty of men out there.

510
00:29:37,110 --> 00:29:39,950
You think she acts like that because she doesn't know?

511
00:29:40,880 --> 00:29:42,190
I mean,

512
00:29:42,550 --> 00:29:44,790
she could just choose one of the other guys.

513
00:29:45,190 --> 00:29:48,160
And Jin Seok has been going straight for Hyo Rim since day one.

514
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:51,830
Why choose a path that's painful and difficult?

515
00:29:51,900 --> 00:29:53,730
That's also part of love.

516
00:29:54,030 --> 00:29:57,530
You wouldn't know. You only ever have fiery romances.

517
00:29:57,630 --> 00:30:00,840
Fiery romances involve crying and all that too.

518
00:30:00,870 --> 00:30:03,440
That's not love, that's just dopamine.

519
00:30:18,290 --> 00:30:20,160
I'm going to look all puffy.

520
00:30:22,060 --> 00:30:24,860
Will you be okay for the interview today?

521
00:30:25,530 --> 00:30:26,930
Yes, I'll try.

522
00:30:29,430 --> 00:30:31,870
Even after your conversation with In Wook today,

523
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:34,200
have your feelings still not changed?

524
00:30:40,480 --> 00:30:42,580
I want to make a choice I won't regret.

525
00:30:45,080 --> 00:30:47,350
Even if my feelings aren't returned.

526
00:30:55,990 --> 00:30:57,489
(It's the day of the final choice.)

527
00:30:57,490 --> 00:30:58,859
(Please place your final Love Chain...)

528
00:30:58,860 --> 00:30:59,899
(on the wrist of the person you choose.)

529
00:30:59,900 --> 00:31:01,330
("Love Chain")

530
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:08,940
All right, now for Song Hyo Rim.

531
00:31:09,310 --> 00:31:11,610
She will now make her final choice.

532
00:31:30,760 --> 00:31:32,160
My final choice is...

533
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:34,400
Seo In Wook.

534
00:31:48,140 --> 00:31:49,150
It's okay.

535
00:31:52,050 --> 00:31:53,280
I'm sorry.

536
00:32:28,890 --> 00:32:29,890
Sa Rang.

537
00:32:36,690 --> 00:32:37,690
Sa Rang.

538
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:40,460
Where are you going?

539
00:32:41,100 --> 00:32:43,970
- I did something terrible. - What did you say?

540
00:32:44,700 --> 00:32:46,840
- I'm really... - Sa Rang.

541
00:32:49,110 --> 00:32:51,140
I'm the worst.

542
00:32:51,770 --> 00:32:53,540
It's not your fault, Sa Rang.

543
00:32:54,380 --> 00:32:57,380
I came on this show for you from the start.

544
00:32:58,110 --> 00:32:59,620
I was arrogant.

545
00:33:01,420 --> 00:33:02,890
So arrogant...

546
00:33:03,550 --> 00:33:05,020
that I deceived everyone.

547
00:33:06,460 --> 00:33:10,190
I thought only my feelings were love, romance, and destiny.

548
00:33:12,030 --> 00:33:13,330
Then what about my feelings?

549
00:33:15,100 --> 00:33:17,730
I understand that you feel sorry for the other contestants.

550
00:33:18,100 --> 00:33:19,470
The feelings I have for you...

551
00:33:20,240 --> 00:33:21,670
What am I supposed to do about them?

552
00:33:28,950 --> 00:33:30,180
I'm sorry.

553
00:33:33,120 --> 00:33:34,580
If you leave me again this time,

554
00:33:35,280 --> 00:33:36,720
then this is the end for me too.

555
00:34:22,600 --> 00:34:24,770
What's wrong with him?

556
00:34:24,830 --> 00:34:26,340
Hey, get out here.

557
00:34:26,500 --> 00:34:28,139
He can't even do it properly,

558
00:34:28,140 --> 00:34:29,740
so why is he getting mixed up with the youngsters...

559
00:34:29,810 --> 00:34:31,070
and making a fool of himself?

560
00:34:31,140 --> 00:34:33,239
Just leave him be. If one competitor is out,

561
00:34:33,240 --> 00:34:35,110
that's great for us. Right?

562
00:34:35,310 --> 00:34:38,550
- Seriously. - Hey. The refrigerator is mine.

563
00:34:38,850 --> 00:34:43,090
- Oh, I can't let you have it. - The MVP prize is a refrigerator?

564
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:44,290
It's right over there.

565
00:34:45,150 --> 00:34:48,690
Well, that changes things.

566
00:34:49,690 --> 00:34:51,430
Do you work out much?

567
00:34:51,760 --> 00:34:52,760
If not for art school,

568
00:34:52,761 --> 00:34:53,900
I would've gone to a sports university.

569
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:56,570
Okay. Got it.

570
00:34:57,600 --> 00:34:59,540
- Hello. - Hello.

571
00:34:59,600 --> 00:35:02,340
- Directors, over here, this way. - Hello, Director.

572
00:35:02,840 --> 00:35:04,270
- You're here. - Yes.

573
00:35:04,340 --> 00:35:05,340
You're here.

574
00:35:05,580 --> 00:35:07,609
Director Woo, you don't seem interested...

575
00:35:07,610 --> 00:35:08,950
in winning a prize today.

576
00:35:09,550 --> 00:35:13,119
I'll just be cheering everyone on. I'm not very competitive.

577
00:35:13,120 --> 00:35:15,690
Director Woo can be the blue team's cheerleader.

578
00:35:16,690 --> 00:35:17,690
Sounds good.

579
00:35:18,020 --> 00:35:19,020
You're wearing a blue shirt.

580
00:35:20,460 --> 00:35:23,360
Oh, here comes the red team's cheerleader.

581
00:35:55,260 --> 00:35:57,430
You all got here early.

582
00:35:57,490 --> 00:36:00,960
Gosh. Looks like a photo at an airport departure gate.

583
00:36:01,030 --> 00:36:03,700
He is a star. I like him.

584
00:36:03,870 --> 00:36:07,400
- What is all this? - Camping is my hobby.

585
00:36:07,970 --> 00:36:10,469
- I brought a few things. - I see.

586
00:36:10,470 --> 00:36:11,540
Just unbelievable. Seriously.

587
00:36:13,740 --> 00:36:14,810
Never mind.

588
00:36:14,880 --> 00:36:16,650
- Good job. - Go easy on us.

589
00:36:16,980 --> 00:36:18,880
- Good game. - I told you to be careful.

590
00:36:29,430 --> 00:36:32,130
- Give it to me. It's heavy. - Thank you.

591
00:36:32,530 --> 00:36:33,530
Chae Yeon.

592
00:36:34,330 --> 00:36:36,170
It's heavy.

593
00:36:37,470 --> 00:36:38,630
Why would he talk to us?

594
00:36:44,810 --> 00:36:46,480
What's in here that makes it so heavy?

595
00:36:48,440 --> 00:36:52,210
Short ribs, skirt steak, ribeye cap, pork jowl, and pork belly.

596
00:36:52,480 --> 00:36:54,380
She prepared all of this.

597
00:36:55,520 --> 00:36:57,220
I'm trying not to be outdone by him.

598
00:36:57,420 --> 00:36:59,420
(Cut! Let's Take a Short Break)

599
00:36:59,920 --> 00:37:01,960
Look. What has he brought this time?

600
00:37:02,990 --> 00:37:04,360
This is great.

601
00:37:05,330 --> 00:37:07,560
- What is this? - This is...

602
00:37:10,470 --> 00:37:11,830
All right, everyone, listen up.

603
00:37:12,900 --> 00:37:15,610
The first game is partner dodgeball.

604
00:37:15,670 --> 00:37:18,440
If you want to play, find a partner and come up here.

605
00:37:18,710 --> 00:37:21,010
- I can't play. My back hurts. - Let's play.

606
00:37:21,080 --> 00:37:23,510
- I have to win that fridge. - Be my partner.

607
00:37:29,020 --> 00:37:30,090
No.

608
00:37:30,650 --> 00:37:31,850
Mu Gyeom will be my partner.

609
00:37:34,290 --> 00:37:36,890
Assistant Director, how about we just get another beer?

610
00:37:38,730 --> 00:37:41,960
- Director Joo, be my partner. - Oh, well...

611
00:37:44,970 --> 00:37:46,140
What's going on?

612
00:37:49,340 --> 00:37:50,840
Gosh, Director.

613
00:37:57,380 --> 00:37:58,410
Director...

614
00:37:59,580 --> 00:38:00,850
Hey, Director Joo.

615
00:38:01,520 --> 00:38:02,549
Beep.

616
00:38:02,550 --> 00:38:06,360
- Director Woo, find a partner. - Right.

617
00:38:24,340 --> 00:38:25,570
With me?

618
00:38:26,580 --> 00:38:27,580
No.

619
00:38:30,080 --> 00:38:32,850
Our target is Geum Seong Moo.

620
00:38:35,050 --> 00:38:36,120
Deal.

621
00:38:37,820 --> 00:38:39,760
Like you're dodging bullets from the Japanese police.

622
00:38:41,120 --> 00:38:42,330
Okay?

623
00:38:43,190 --> 00:38:45,660
- Yes. - Mu Gyeom, our independence... No.

624
00:38:46,130 --> 00:38:49,870
- The fridge is riding on it. Okay? - Got it.

625
00:38:50,470 --> 00:38:51,470
(Woo Su Bin, Director)

626
00:38:52,130 --> 00:38:53,300
(Geum Seong Moo, Actor playing Crow)

627
00:39:01,140 --> 00:39:02,650
Are you any good at dodgeball?

628
00:39:02,710 --> 00:39:05,980
Don't worry. I'll keep Director Joo safe.

629
00:39:06,650 --> 00:39:09,750
- Let's do this. - Protect her? Worry about yourself.

630
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:16,590
Why you...

631
00:39:32,910 --> 00:39:34,280
Two o'clock.

632
00:39:35,280 --> 00:39:36,649
Whatever you do, don't hit Director Joo.

633
00:39:36,650 --> 00:39:38,250
We have to hit Geum Seong Moo.

634
00:39:39,520 --> 00:39:40,820
Don't worry.

635
00:39:46,560 --> 00:39:47,590
Seong Moo.

636
00:39:48,260 --> 00:39:50,230
Director of Photography. You're out.

637
00:39:50,290 --> 00:39:52,660
It's fine. Mu Gyeom can just buy me the fridge.

638
00:40:04,970 --> 00:40:06,110
Come on!

639
00:40:14,280 --> 00:40:15,380
Darn it.

640
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:30,030
What's going on?

641
00:40:35,570 --> 00:40:37,940
But other teams are still in, you know.

642
00:40:38,310 --> 00:40:40,240
- Hold on tight. - Wait...

643
00:40:50,290 --> 00:40:51,490
Are you okay?

644
00:40:52,520 --> 00:40:55,420
Director Woo, you have been separated from your partner.

645
00:40:57,290 --> 00:40:58,660
You're out.

646
00:41:01,100 --> 00:41:02,100
Dummy.

647
00:41:02,900 --> 00:41:03,900
That's not important.

648
00:41:04,500 --> 00:41:05,870
Can you get up?

649
00:41:21,450 --> 00:41:23,450
(Driver's License Written Test)

650
00:41:26,660 --> 00:41:30,830
- I'll be back. - Did you take your pencil case?

651
00:41:31,960 --> 00:41:33,899
They use computers these days.

652
00:41:33,900 --> 00:41:35,800
- Isn't it cool? - They do?

653
00:41:36,970 --> 00:41:38,500
Will you be all right on your own?

654
00:41:38,570 --> 00:41:40,540
You can barely walk around the neighbourhood.

655
00:41:40,600 --> 00:41:43,170
- I'm not a child. - Just wait a minute.

656
00:41:44,270 --> 00:41:45,370
Let me...

657
00:41:46,310 --> 00:41:49,480
walk you to the bus stop.

658
00:41:49,510 --> 00:41:52,250
If you walk with me, I'll miss that bus.

659
00:41:53,080 --> 00:41:54,250
You should rest.

660
00:41:55,480 --> 00:41:56,790
I'm going.

661
00:42:30,420 --> 00:42:31,690
Ma'am.

662
00:42:32,590 --> 00:42:34,190
You're Su Bin's mother, right?

663
00:42:34,520 --> 00:42:36,860
- Jin Su? - Are you all right?

664
00:42:39,330 --> 00:42:41,800
- Do you need some help? - No, it's fine.

665
00:42:44,100 --> 00:42:45,630
Ma'am, where are you headed?

666
00:42:46,170 --> 00:42:49,069
I'm going to take my driver's test.

667
00:42:49,070 --> 00:42:50,910
I need to catch the bus.

668
00:42:51,370 --> 00:42:53,080
Then you'll have to go to Baemun-dong.

669
00:42:53,480 --> 00:42:56,210
- I can give you a ride. - Really?

670
00:42:56,780 --> 00:42:57,980
Would that be okay?

671
00:42:58,050 --> 00:43:00,420
I'm heading that way anyway. Get in.

672
00:43:00,480 --> 00:43:02,180
- Okay, thank you. - Yes, get in.

673
00:43:05,390 --> 00:43:06,720
- Thanks. - Sure.

674
00:43:08,720 --> 00:43:12,160
I'll get you there safely.

675
00:43:26,680 --> 00:43:29,510
She's showing off again. Oh, honestly.

676
00:43:32,480 --> 00:43:33,720
What did she post?

677
00:43:38,890 --> 00:43:40,060
What's this?

678
00:43:40,460 --> 00:43:41,720
(You sure make a big show out of donating.)

679
00:43:42,020 --> 00:43:46,300
Darn it. Who the heck posted this picture?

680
00:43:46,630 --> 00:43:47,930
Unbelievable.

681
00:43:47,960 --> 00:43:49,230
(A big donation, and an even bigger after-party)

682
00:43:49,330 --> 00:43:51,430
Oh, for goodness' sake. Gosh.

683
00:43:52,670 --> 00:43:53,970
Director Kim.

684
00:43:54,970 --> 00:43:56,610
Hey, Director Kim!

685
00:44:00,580 --> 00:44:03,750
Hey, you son of a witch. Open the door.

686
00:44:03,810 --> 00:44:05,580
You're so dead.

687
00:44:08,820 --> 00:44:10,920
Oh, darn it. You son of a witch.

688
00:44:11,390 --> 00:44:13,190
How can you be sleeping at a time like this?

689
00:44:13,220 --> 00:44:16,160
- What's wrong? What happened? - Get to the office. Now.

690
00:44:16,860 --> 00:44:19,030
PR team, they're dead meat.

691
00:44:19,090 --> 00:44:21,330
What trouble did they cause this time?

692
00:44:21,460 --> 00:44:23,930
CEO Ahn. This is why I can never take a day off.

693
00:44:23,970 --> 00:44:26,540
You're dead too, Director Kang.

694
00:44:27,370 --> 00:44:29,170
- Go, now! - Right.

695
00:44:30,210 --> 00:44:31,710
You son of a witch. What were you doing...

696
00:44:31,770 --> 00:44:33,440
with your feet on the steering wheel?

697
00:44:33,510 --> 00:44:35,180
Ma'am, put on your seatbelt.

698
00:44:43,050 --> 00:44:44,050
All of you.

699
00:44:44,590 --> 00:44:47,190
This was a private party. I said not to post anywhere.

700
00:44:47,260 --> 00:44:48,260
Did you hear me or not?

701
00:44:48,620 --> 00:44:49,790
Well, we...

702
00:44:50,790 --> 00:44:52,090
Yes, we heard you.

703
00:44:52,530 --> 00:44:53,960
But you posted it anyway?

704
00:44:54,460 --> 00:44:55,460
Who was it?

705
00:44:56,830 --> 00:44:59,130
Who's so desperate to take me down?

706
00:45:00,140 --> 00:45:01,140
Was it you?

707
00:45:02,840 --> 00:45:03,840
Was it you?

708
00:45:04,910 --> 00:45:07,939
Come on. There's no need for that.

709
00:45:07,940 --> 00:45:09,410
It was just a mistake by some clueless employees...

710
00:45:10,610 --> 00:45:12,680
You ignorant fool. You're the biggest problem here.

711
00:45:12,750 --> 00:45:14,250
You can't even manage these idiots.

712
00:45:14,480 --> 00:45:16,220
What is it you do around here?

713
00:45:18,390 --> 00:45:20,360
Ma'am, not in front of the team...

714
00:45:20,420 --> 00:45:23,060
So what? Oh, is your pride hurt?

715
00:45:23,690 --> 00:45:24,730
Ma'am.

716
00:45:25,030 --> 00:45:28,660
Honestly, just keeping up with your schedule is overwhelming.

717
00:45:28,800 --> 00:45:30,470
I'm not your personal manager.

718
00:45:30,530 --> 00:45:32,430
All I do is drive you around and run your errands.

719
00:45:32,900 --> 00:45:35,700
I don't even know what my job is at this company anymore.

720
00:45:35,800 --> 00:45:36,910
Oh, my, Director Kang.

721
00:45:38,510 --> 00:45:41,110
You're the one who said you'd do anything I asked.

722
00:45:41,180 --> 00:45:43,250
You were crying your eyes out with nowhere to go,

723
00:45:43,310 --> 00:45:44,610
and I was the one who took you in.

724
00:45:44,980 --> 00:45:47,450
Now that life is a little easier, have you lost your mind?

725
00:45:48,020 --> 00:45:50,320
Want to go back to when you were barely scraping by?

726
00:45:57,730 --> 00:45:59,230
Director Kang, are you okay?

727
00:46:00,900 --> 00:46:04,070
Seriously, CEO Ahn. What century does she think this is?

728
00:46:04,170 --> 00:46:05,430
That's what I'm saying.

729
00:46:06,370 --> 00:46:10,840
I mean, she treats you like a pushover.

730
00:46:15,010 --> 00:46:17,750
But are you going to keep working for CEO Ahn?

731
00:46:18,550 --> 00:46:20,880
If I were you, I'd have left and started my own company ages ago.

732
00:46:20,980 --> 00:46:23,920
That's right. CEO Ahn needs to feel what it's like when you're gone.

733
00:46:23,990 --> 00:46:24,990
Right.

734
00:46:25,520 --> 00:46:26,690
Oh, you think so?

735
00:46:27,490 --> 00:46:30,160
- You all think so too? - Of course. Absolutely.

736
00:46:30,590 --> 00:46:33,060
Then I'll follow you no matter what, Director Kang.

737
00:47:19,880 --> 00:47:21,880
- Be careful. - Watch out.

738
00:47:33,590 --> 00:47:37,160
Our hard-working director. Open your mouth.

739
00:47:43,330 --> 00:47:44,330
Is that for me?

740
00:47:47,570 --> 00:47:49,940
You've been working so hard. Here, have a bite.

741
00:47:51,110 --> 00:47:52,809
- I don't have a free hand. - Right.

742
00:47:52,810 --> 00:47:53,940
Hey, give it to me.

743
00:47:58,380 --> 00:47:59,450
It's delicious.

744
00:47:59,780 --> 00:48:01,150
- Thanks, Director Joo. - Sure.

745
00:48:02,950 --> 00:48:04,090
I'm not doing this.

746
00:48:07,290 --> 00:48:08,560
Then I'll grill the meat.

747
00:48:09,360 --> 00:48:10,390
Forget it.

748
00:48:11,290 --> 00:48:12,290
Go eat.

749
00:48:12,330 --> 00:48:14,430
I came here specifically to avoid that table.

750
00:48:15,030 --> 00:48:16,030
What?

751
00:48:26,280 --> 00:48:27,310
You should stop drinking.

752
00:48:28,110 --> 00:48:29,210
You've had too much to drink.

753
00:48:29,540 --> 00:48:31,350
Let me get drunk for once.

754
00:48:32,910 --> 00:48:34,980
I wonder how far I can go using being drunk as an excuse.

755
00:48:37,390 --> 00:48:38,390
Give it to me.

756
00:49:02,410 --> 00:49:03,410
Goodbye.

757
00:49:16,390 --> 00:49:19,390
Hey, are you okay? You were really knocking them back.

758
00:49:20,200 --> 00:49:21,200
Where's Ha Na?

759
00:49:22,630 --> 00:49:24,830
I haven't seen her. Have you?

760
00:49:25,630 --> 00:49:27,840
- Did you see her? - No.

761
00:49:34,640 --> 00:49:35,640
Hey, where are you going?

762
00:49:38,210 --> 00:49:39,680
Chae Yeon.

763
00:49:40,880 --> 00:49:42,580
Could you please give this to Ha Na?

764
00:49:43,990 --> 00:49:45,750
- What's this? - She'll feel rough tomorrow.

765
00:49:45,990 --> 00:49:49,890
But wasn't Ha Na with you?

766
00:49:52,260 --> 00:49:54,060
She's not inside?

767
00:49:54,660 --> 00:49:55,660
No.

768
00:49:59,970 --> 00:50:00,970
Darn it.

769
00:50:03,510 --> 00:50:05,840
- Hello. - Hi.

770
00:50:08,780 --> 00:50:09,950
We've been waiting for you.

771
00:50:10,880 --> 00:50:12,910
- Oh, my. - Are you looking for something?

772
00:50:12,980 --> 00:50:13,980
- No, it's nothing. - Come in.

773
00:50:14,050 --> 00:50:15,150
- Come in and have a drink. - No, thank you.

774
00:50:15,220 --> 00:50:16,220
- Have a drink. - Enjoy yourselves.

775
00:50:39,370 --> 00:50:40,380
What are you doing here?

776
00:50:41,280 --> 00:50:42,510
Punishing you.

777
00:50:47,050 --> 00:50:48,080
Let's go.

778
00:50:48,850 --> 00:50:51,090
- Your manager's worried about you. - What about you?

779
00:50:54,390 --> 00:50:56,120
You came because you were worried about me too.

780
00:50:58,690 --> 00:51:00,600
I'd be worried about anyone out here.

781
00:51:12,940 --> 00:51:14,680
It's just the two of us here.

782
00:51:16,580 --> 00:51:19,950
My mom isn't here, and neither is the crew.

783
00:51:22,120 --> 00:51:24,020
There's no one watching us.

784
00:51:25,720 --> 00:51:27,120
So you can be honest.

785
00:51:27,860 --> 00:51:29,160
Like that time at the lodging.

786
00:51:54,620 --> 00:51:55,620
Forget it.

787
00:51:59,220 --> 00:52:00,690
- I'll walk you back. - Don't touch me!

788
00:52:02,060 --> 00:52:03,230
You coward.

789
00:52:17,540 --> 00:52:21,810
Hey. Where on earth have you been? I've been looking all over for you.

790
00:52:22,480 --> 00:52:25,350
It was snowing so hard earlier. Why were you wandering around?

791
00:52:25,410 --> 00:52:27,180
Didn't I tell you to let me know whenever you go somewhere?

792
00:52:29,020 --> 00:52:31,850
Wait a minute. Why is your face so red?

793
00:52:41,660 --> 00:52:42,830
Meet me at the Observation Deck.

794
00:52:42,930 --> 00:52:44,370
(Meet me at the Observation Deck.)

795
00:52:45,230 --> 00:52:46,230
Director Joo.

796
00:52:48,240 --> 00:52:50,370
What are you doing here?

797
00:52:51,470 --> 00:52:52,470
Thinking about you.

798
00:52:53,070 --> 00:52:54,240
Come on.

799
00:52:54,610 --> 00:52:55,840
We're not on set.

800
00:52:56,610 --> 00:52:58,710
We don't have to be a director and an actor, right?

801
00:53:00,480 --> 00:53:03,290
All right, then. Fine. Then I'll be on my way.

802
00:53:03,820 --> 00:53:04,820
Don't you remember this place?

803
00:53:06,660 --> 00:53:08,289
Every time you tried to break up with me,

804
00:53:08,290 --> 00:53:10,160
I'd bring you here and show you the stars.

805
00:53:10,960 --> 00:53:12,730
This is that place?

806
00:53:13,400 --> 00:53:16,770
You'd always say, "I'll be your star."

807
00:53:17,100 --> 00:53:18,270
And you'd refuse to let me go.

808
00:53:18,870 --> 00:53:19,900
Yes.

809
00:53:20,240 --> 00:53:21,270
You really didn't know?

810
00:53:22,070 --> 00:53:23,070
Well, I guess that makes sense.

811
00:53:23,970 --> 00:53:26,980
Back then, it was just a quiet, empty forest.

812
00:53:29,280 --> 00:53:32,550
There aren't any stars either. There used to be so many back then.

813
00:53:35,480 --> 00:53:36,480
You're right.

814
00:53:37,390 --> 00:53:38,920
It seemed like they would pour down on us back then.

815
00:53:42,360 --> 00:53:43,360
Yi Jae.

816
00:53:46,290 --> 00:53:48,400
This forest became a glamping site,

817
00:53:49,200 --> 00:53:51,800
and all those stars have now grown faint.

818
00:53:54,440 --> 00:53:55,970
But whether it was ten years ago or now,

819
00:53:56,640 --> 00:53:57,940
I still feel the same way about you.

820
00:53:59,610 --> 00:54:01,680
- Listen, I... - You see,

821
00:54:03,010 --> 00:54:06,050
my heart still aches whenever I think of you.

822
00:54:07,450 --> 00:54:08,680
You and I...

823
00:54:09,620 --> 00:54:12,220
met when we were struggling and had nothing,

824
00:54:12,920 --> 00:54:13,920
remember?

825
00:54:15,960 --> 00:54:16,990
Now,

826
00:54:17,490 --> 00:54:19,530
don't you think things will be different from then?

827
00:54:19,890 --> 00:54:21,959
Seong Moo, you know full well what's going on.

828
00:54:21,960 --> 00:54:23,100
Are you doing this on purpose?

829
00:54:31,810 --> 00:54:32,840
So...

830
00:54:33,880 --> 00:54:35,140
are you still not over your first love?

831
00:54:37,250 --> 00:54:38,480
Seong Moo, listen.

832
00:54:40,050 --> 00:54:41,150
I still...

833
00:54:41,980 --> 00:54:43,050
and always...

834
00:54:43,920 --> 00:54:45,120
like Woo Su Bin.

835
00:54:54,960 --> 00:54:56,430
Why are you making that confession here?

836
00:54:57,170 --> 00:54:58,170
Woo Su Bin.

837
00:55:01,470 --> 00:55:02,970
As you can see, what's between Yi Jae and me...

838
00:55:04,110 --> 00:55:05,440
is not a first love that's in the past.

839
00:55:06,640 --> 00:55:08,810
I stayed quiet because you didn't know,

840
00:55:09,110 --> 00:55:10,410
but now that you do.

841
00:55:11,510 --> 00:55:12,750
So I'd appreciate it if you stopped...

842
00:55:13,620 --> 00:55:14,680
crossing the line.

843
00:55:17,990 --> 00:55:19,990
- Let's go. - Okay.

844
00:55:53,350 --> 00:55:54,689
Ready.

845
00:55:54,690 --> 00:55:55,720
Action!

846
00:55:57,860 --> 00:55:58,860
Hey!

847
00:55:59,790 --> 00:56:00,800
You!

848
00:56:06,970 --> 00:56:08,970
- Get him! - Stop!

849
00:56:31,030 --> 00:56:32,030
Cut.

850
00:56:34,060 --> 00:56:35,230
Why is it so noisy?

851
00:56:35,700 --> 00:56:36,770
I'll go and check.

852
00:56:38,170 --> 00:56:40,470
Yes, CEO Ahn. We're in the middle of filming.

853
00:56:42,140 --> 00:56:44,510
What? What did you say?

854
00:56:45,940 --> 00:56:46,940
Director Woo.

855
00:56:51,110 --> 00:56:54,050
Who said I was barging in? I'm here to see Director Ian.

856
00:56:54,120 --> 00:56:55,620
But that means you're trying to go in now.

857
00:56:55,680 --> 00:56:57,750
- You can't. - Is Actress Oh Ha Na in there too?

858
00:56:59,420 --> 00:57:01,060
What do you think you're doing now?

859
00:57:02,920 --> 00:57:05,660
What gives you the right to just barge onto a film set?

860
00:57:05,730 --> 00:57:06,730
Director Ian!

861
00:57:08,760 --> 00:57:10,970
Is it true you're CEO Ahn Soo Hee's secret son?

862
00:57:11,200 --> 00:57:14,300
Can you confirm the reports that you were born out of an affair?

863
00:57:14,370 --> 00:57:15,370
Are you admitting it?

864
00:57:15,940 --> 00:57:16,940
Did you know about this?

865
00:57:17,040 --> 00:57:18,310
Is there something more to this story?

866
00:57:18,370 --> 00:57:20,680
- Are you admitting it? - Please give us a statement.

867
00:57:21,540 --> 00:57:23,810
- What does that mean? - Actress Oh Ha Na?

868
00:57:24,550 --> 00:57:26,510
- Oh Ha Na? - It's Oh Ha Na.

869
00:57:26,920 --> 00:57:28,820
- It's Oh Ha Na. - It's Oh Ha Na.

870
00:57:31,450 --> 00:57:34,290
An audio file of your mother, Ahn Soo Hee, has been released.

871
00:57:34,560 --> 00:57:36,859
Did you by any chance know...

872
00:57:36,860 --> 00:57:38,860
that you and Director Ian are half-siblings?

873
00:57:40,300 --> 00:57:42,100
Is it true you and Director Ian Woo are siblings?

874
00:57:43,260 --> 00:57:44,270
- What? - Please comment, Oh Ha Na.

875
00:57:44,330 --> 00:57:45,370
- Oh Ha Na, anything to say? - Give us a statement.

876
00:57:45,430 --> 00:57:47,270
Director Ian, please give us a statement.

877
00:57:47,340 --> 00:57:48,640
- Please look this way. - What is your relationship?

878
00:57:48,700 --> 00:57:49,700
Oh Ha Na, please look over here.

879
00:57:49,770 --> 00:57:51,909
What are your thoughts on the casting favouritism controversy?

880
00:57:51,910 --> 00:57:53,040
Oh Ha Na?

881
00:58:11,890 --> 00:58:13,760
(Special thanks to Lee Joo Ahn for his special appearance)

882
00:58:42,090 --> 00:58:44,060
(Dream To You)

883
00:58:44,760 --> 00:58:45,860
Let go!

884
00:58:46,900 --> 00:58:49,529
- Before I go and kill myself. - I can do this, right?

885
00:58:49,530 --> 00:58:51,700
It's my first time alone without Director Woo.

886
00:58:51,770 --> 00:58:53,769
It's okay, Yi Jae. Stay calm.

887
00:58:53,770 --> 00:58:56,100
You have to make a decision now. Otherwise,

888
00:58:56,170 --> 00:58:59,410
- they'll halt filming immediately. - Director Joo!

889
00:58:59,840 --> 00:59:02,440
As the director, I am deeply sorry.

890
00:59:02,880 --> 00:59:05,380
Don't worry. I'll fix everything.

891
00:59:05,910 --> 00:59:07,080
If I step down,

892
00:59:07,450 --> 00:59:09,950
can Director Joo Yi Jae continue with the film as planned?